      <Comment source="SRI, caspi">An aldehyde is an organic compound containing a formyl group (CHO). This functional group consists of a carbonyl centre bonded to hydrogen and an R group. Aldehydes differ from |FRAME: LONG-CHAIN-KETONE ketones| in that the carbonyl is placed at the end of a carbon skeleton rather than between two carbon atoms.</Comment>
